IVE - Integrated Vibe Editor

The colour values in assets/schemes/ and the Java, JSON, YAML, TOML, HTML, XML, Markdown, Shell Script, Python,
Kotlin, Groovy, Properties and RegExp texts in assets/previews/ are ported from IntelliJ IDEA Community Edition
(https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-community), Copyright 2000-2026 JetBrains s.r.o. and contributors, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

The highlight and injection queries in assets/queries/ started from the queries of the tree-sitter grammars they
are written for (MIT License, except tree-sitter-fish: The Unlicense).

vendor/grammars/ holds the generated parsers of six tree-sitter grammars, unchanged; each folder has the upstream
LICENSE and a SOURCE file naming the repository and commit:
- dockerfile: https://github.com/camdencheek/tree-sitter-dockerfile (MIT License)
- fish: https://github.com/ram02z/tree-sitter-fish (The Unlicense)
- gomod: https://github.com/camdencheek/tree-sitter-go-mod (MIT License)
- scss: https://github.com/tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-scss (MIT License)
- sql: https://github.com/DerekStride/tree-sitter-sql (MIT License)
- vue: https://github.com/tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-vue (MIT License)

vendor/grammars/rune is IVE's Rune grammar: its grammar.js extends tree-sitter-rust's
(https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust, MIT License), copied unchanged as rust.js with that grammar's
LICENSE; src/scanner.c is tree-sitter-rust's scanner with its functions renamed, src/parser.c is generated.

vendor/conpty/ holds conpty.dll and OpenConsole.exe (x64) from Microsoft's NuGet package
Microsoft.Windows.Console.ConPTY, built from https://github.com/microsoft/terminal (MIT License), unchanged; the
Windows build copies them next to ive.exe. The folder has the upstream LICENSE and a SOURCE file naming the version;
Windows releases carry that LICENSE as licenses/conpty-LICENSE.

The icons in assets/icons/ are from the IntelliJ Platform New UI icon set, Copyright 2000-2022 JetBrains s.r.o. and
contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; assets/icons/NOTICE says which are modified or drawn
for IVE, and assets/icons/LICENSE holds the licence.

assets/fonts/ bundles Inter (Copyright 2020 The Inter Project Authors, https://github.com/rsms/inter) and
JetBrains Mono (Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors, https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono),
both under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (assets/fonts/*-OFL.txt).

gpui and its crates come from Zed (https://github.com/zed-industries/zed), Copyright Zed Industries, Inc., licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0, through https://github.com/Warsaw-Dynamics/pgui (branch zed-main), which
modifies crates/gpui/src/text_system.rs and crates/gpui_wgpu/src/cosmic_text_system.rs so a colour emoji font can be
a font fallback on Linux.

libgit2 (built into the git2 crate) is licensed under the GNU General Public License, Version 2, with a linking
exception that allows linking it unmodified into programs under any licence: licenses/libgit2-COPYING, which also
holds the notices of the code bundled with libgit2. Source: https://github.com/libgit2/libgit2.

The Rust crates IVE is built from, with their licence texts, are listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
(tools/third-party-notices.sh); deny.toml lists the licences they may use.
